alse}, {"t_ms": 14434, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01V4ynWGw4uHjMEuYpAdoAM5", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 23874, "event": "escalation", "actor": "control_plane", "id": "esc1", "kind": "clarification", "trigger": "principal_reply", "tool": null, "args": null, "question": "I haven't rolled anything back or opened the incident yet. There's no service called `payments`, and two payments services are unhealthy, so I need you to tell me which one you mean.\n\n| Service | Current version | Health | Error rate | Last healthy production release |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `payments-api` | v5.1.0 (all regions) | degraded | 18% | **v5.0.0** |\n| `payments-worker` | v3.4.0 (all regions) | unhealthy | 18% | **v3.3.0** |\n\nBoth had a new version deployed after their last healthy release. The deployment history doesn't include timestamps, so I can't tell which one went out this morning. You asked for one service to be rolled back, and a rollback hits every production region, so I didn't want to guess or roll back both without checking. There are no open incidents right now.\n\nWhich should I do?\n1. Roll back `payments-api` to v5.0.0\n2. Roll back `payments-worker` to v3.3.0\n3. Roll back both\n\nOnce you pick, I'll do the rollback and open a SEV2 incident for that service right away. Both target versions were healthy in production, so neither rollback needs change-manager approval.", "context": {}}, {"t_ms": 136576, "event": "human_response", "actor": "human", "escalation": "esc1", "decision": "answer", "message": "It's payments-worker - the API errors are downstream of the worker.", "latency_ms": 112702, "hint": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "erred": false}, {"t_ms": 136576, "event": "principal_reply", "actor": "human", "text": "It's payments-worker - the API errors are downstream of the worker."}, {"t_ms": 139465, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01FXuBSs9578YLJeePKVq5Pi", "tool": "rollback", "args": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 143465, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01FXuBSs9578YLJeePKVq5Pi", "tool": "rollback", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 143465, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01FXuBSs9578YLJeePKVq5Pi", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 148278, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_014PTwTWrcAfQyza111ic2bV", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "payments-worker errors after v3.4.0 deploy; rolled back to v3.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "payments-worker v3.4.0 (deployed this morning) was unhealthy in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an ~18% error rate. Downstream impact: payments-api (v5.1.0) also degraded at ~18% error rate; the user reports the API errors are downstream of the worker. Action taken: payments-worker rolled back to v3.3.0, its last healthy production release, in all regions. Next steps: confirm the worker and payments-api error rates recover, and investigate the v3.4.0 regression.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 148878, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_014PTwTWrcAfQyza111ic2bV", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 148878, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_014PTwTWrcAfQyza111ic2bV", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 148878, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_0158hTZuy9Sz1eAnXqQ6scsq", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 149178, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_0158hTZuy9Sz1eAnXqQ6scsq", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 149178, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0158hTZuy9Sz1eAnXqQ6scsq", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 149178, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_013cSd5wJGExKnFbeAbpRqNn", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "payments-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 149478, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_013cSd5wJGExKnFbeAbpRqNn", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 149478, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_013cSd5wJGExKnFbeAbpRqNn", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 154772, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled `payments-worker` back to v3.3.0 and opened the SEV2 incident. The worker has recovered, but `payments-api` is still failing.\n\n1. **Rollback:** `payments-worker` went from v3.4.0 to v3.3.0, its most recent release that was healthy in production. It's confirmed live in us-east, us-west and eu-west. Its error rate fell from 18% to 0.2%, and it now reports healthy.\n2. **Incident:** **INC-0001** (SEV2) is open for `payments-worker`, and on-call has been paged. It records the bad release, the rollback and the effect on `payments-api`.\n\n**`payments-api` is still unhealthy** on v5.1.0, with an 18% error rate, right after the worker rollback. It may just need time to recover. If it stays at that level, the problem may not be only downstream of the worker. v5.1.0 could have its own regression, or the API may need a restart or to work through a backlog.\n\nYou asked me to roll back only the worker, so I haven't touched `payments-api`. If its errors don't drop soon, I can roll it back to v5.0.0, its last healthy production release, which doesn't need change-manager approval. I can also add this finding to INC-0001 for on-call.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GjWz9ZekN21wL78oi9RhhY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_013xW5rg7WgDPRQfba1kGSeP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_016gKF83feyLAAPBb5t3Dtsj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_018pMvK4y6VknmvTUj9fkRZJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_018p2xdVcDFh8arQnmv6PnwB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-service"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Kbw4jKNeXk75uRpphtxpik", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01MNasNnvKjpY9B1EEby9zf3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01XHf6EVNWQG5dg